        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Canaanite religion</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 3000 BCE – c. 400 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Origin</span><span class="info-stat-val">the land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canaan">Canaan</a> in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>, during approximately the first three millennia BCE; first attested in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebla">Ebla</a> tablets of the second half of the 3rd millennium BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founder or early teachers</span><span class="info-stat-val">none: a tradition of many peoples and cities, strongly influenced by its Egyptian and Mesopotamian neighbours</span></div>
